extensions/*/sirsi

# Idea Router runtime artifacts
.agents/idea-router/bin/
.agents/idea-router/work-queue.json
.agents/idea-router/threads.json
.agents/idea-router/logs/
.agents/idea-router/.threads.json-*
.agents/idea-router/processes.json
.agents/idea-router/board.json
# Per-agent runtime cursors and alarm stamps. These are written continuously by
# `sirsi router wait` and the police duty — one file per agent, rewritten on
# every wake. They are machine state, never source.
#
# Untracked is NOT harmless here: Go's buildvcs stamps `vcs.modified` from
# `git status --porcelain`, which counts UNTRACKED files. So these alone kept
# every build on the conduit host marked DIRTY, which tripped
# `routerstore: refusing to migrate v0->v1 from a build with uncommitted
# changes` and failed every cmd/sirsi test — blocking the Ma'at pre-push gate
# for any change touching that package. The test failures were environmental,
# never caused by the code under test.
.agents/idea-router/.wait-cursor-*
.agents/idea-router/police/.last-alarm-*
# Runtime router state that lives beside the corpus. state.json is already
# untracked on main (88dff818 "untrack all router runtime files"); naming it
# here stops it being re-added by accident, which is how it came to be tracked
# on a side branch and then DELETED by a checkout back to main — taking the
# fabric down with it (router doctor failed outright, 2026-08-06).
.agents/idea-router/state.json
.agents/idea-router/requests/
.agents/idea-router/results/
.agents/idea-router/status/
.agents/idea-router/.board-*.json
.agents/idea-router/locks/
# Router messages are EPHEMERAL per-machine runtime state (like the queue/registry
# above), not source. Tracking them churned the worktree (hundreds of modified
# .md every session) and is the "dirty status" operator clutter. Ignore + untrack.
.agents/idea-router/items/

# Claude local runtime artifacts
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (isolated, never tracked)
.claude/worktrees/

# Idea-router review artifacts — ephemeral runtime output, local-only
.agents/idea-router/reviews/

# Understand-Anything generated graph cache — large, churns every run, derived
# from source. Regenerated by /understand; keep meta.json/.understandignore only.
.understand-anything/fingerprints.json
.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json

# Bind identity private keys (ADR-041) — the sirsi-bind App key is local-only,
# never committed and never a GitHub Secret. A key in CI lets a PR approve itself.
*.pem
.agents/idea-router/police/*.log

# Ad-hoc scratch worktrees agents create directly at repo root (not registered
# via `git worktree add`, so `git worktree list` never sees them and they
# never appear on the removal path). Found dirtying the primary worktree
# 2026-08-06 while diagnosing why every push failed the Ma'at pre-push gate:
# Go's -buildvcs stamps vcs.modified from `git status --porcelain`, which
# counts these same as any other untracked file.
.codex-pr545/
worktrees/
